NAME
       xargs - build command lines from standard input

SYNOPSIS
       xargs [-n max] [-I repl] [command [args...]]

DESCRIPTION
       Reads whitespace-separated words from standard input and runs
       COMMAND with them appended. Without COMMAND, echo is used.

OPTIONS
       -n N   pass at most N arguments per command line
       -I R   run the command once per input line, replacing R in the
              arguments with that line

EXAMPLES
       find /mnt -name '*.tmp' | xargs rm -f
       ls *.png | xargs -I{} cp {} /mnt/pics/

SEE ALSO
       find(1), seq(1)
